            {
              "id": "a904f894-00e3-4acc-9594-55c030f25d2b",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>The Play of the Platonic Dialogues</strong></em> was written by Bernard Freydberg, published by Peter Lang Inc., June 1, 1997."
            },
            {
              "id": "cf6956ab-3402-4ee8-9471-e1e6a4684137",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "5d1f641f-a160-4cec-b65d-4671390d2387",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Play resides at the heart of the </em><a href=\"#/plato\"><em>Platonic</em></a><em> dialogues, shaping their insights as well as informing their style. </em>The Play of the Platonic Dialogues <em>traces the prominent role of play, both as a general philosophical characteristic and as influencing the treatment of key issues. The nature of the forms, of the city, of virtue, of the soul and its immortality - these and others have been shaped by play. This book shows how Platonic </em><a href=\"#/is-the-homo-ludens-cheerful-and-serious-at-the-same-time\"><em>playfulness is joined with the deepest seriousness</em></a><em> throughout the dialogues.</em>"
            }
          ]
        },
